## Why This Is Asked
Tests for autosave/drafts cover offline-first UX, idempotent writes, and cross-device conflicts, which are common pain points in real apps.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first data flows and write queuing
- Idempotent REST writes and ordering guarantees
- Test data isolation via seeds and reset hooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright skeleton (pseudo)
test('autosave offline queue and merge', async ({ page, request }) => {
  await page.goto('/editor');
  await page.fill('#note', 'Initial');
  await page.waitForTimeout(31000); // wait for autosave
  // simulate offline
  await page.route('POST', '/api/drafts', route => route.abort());
  await page.fill('#note', 'Offline edit');
  await page.setOfflineMode(true);
  await page.fill('#note', 'More offline edits');
  await page.setOfflineMode(false);
  // verify upload order and no duplicates
  // reload or inspect draft store
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for WebSocket-based drafting?
- How would you test long offline periods and partial merges?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests that simulate real user journeys in security-sensitive flows, like passwordless login, reveal how teams handle token security, expiry, and multi-device sessions under deterministic conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Passwordless authentication flows
- One-time tokens and expiry windows
- Session management across devices
- Test isolation with mocked email provider
- Deterministic timing for flaky-edge cases

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright sketch
test('passwordless login end-to-end', async ({ page, request }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.fill('#email', 'user@example.com');
  await page.click('#send-link');
  // intercept and extract magic link from mocked email API
  const link = await getMagicLinkFromEmail('user@example.com');
  await page.goto(link);
  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/dashboard');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test token revocation across multiple browsers and devices?
- How would you simulate clock skew or expiry boundary conditions in CI?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes the candidate's ability to design E2E tests for multi-tenant, event-driven systems with cross-region replication. It also looks for strategies to achieve determinism via mocks.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing for multi-tenant apps
- Data isolation and fixture management
- Mocking external storage and network conditions
- Idempotency and eventual consistency under partition
- Observability and retry semantics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright skeleton for the described flow
test('multi-tenant project Creation E2E', async ({ page, context }) => {
  await loginAsTenant('A');
  await createProject('A', { name: 'ProjX' });
  await inviteCollaborator('A', 'user@example.com');
  await uploadBlob('A', 'ProjX/spec.pdf');
  // duplicate event to test idempotency
  await createProject('A', { name: 'ProjX' });
  await verifyRegionReplication('A', 'Region1', 'ProjX');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you structure test data factories for multi-tenant isolation?
- How would you monitor flaky tests and ensure stability when simulating cross-region delays?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests integration with external services and resilience of orchestration under latency/outages; validates end-to-end visibility and data isolation.

## Key Concepts

- E2E with external service mocks
- Event-driven workflow orchestration
- Idempotency and retries
- Data seeds and tenant isolation
- Observability and tracing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test outline for Playwright/Cypress
const seed = createTenantSeed('tenantA');
mockJiraAPI(seed);
mockSlackWebhook(seed);
startFlow('/api/flow', {tenant: 'tenantA', data: seed.payload});
await expect(jiraIssue(seed.issueKey)).toBeOpenOrInProgress();
await slackChannelHasMessage(seed.channel, seed.issueLink);
triggerApproval(seed.approvalId);
await expect(jiraIssue(seed.issueKey)).toHaveStatus('Done');
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify end-to-end latency budgets across regions?
- How handle partially failing external services and ensure idempotent retries?
